    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: reject owner creation at the daily limit (429)\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint is an OfficeFloor function pipeline. I added a new reject step mirroring the existing `RejectCityAtCapacity` pattern:\n\n**New files**\n- `RejectOverDailyLimit.java` \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today; throws `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` when the count is \u2265 100. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created isn't counted.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause for OfficeFloor escalation).\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the other escalation handlers.\n- `...escalation.DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Edited**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `rejectOverDailyLimit` step (governed by the same transaction) between `rejectCityAtCapacity` and `assignHousehold`.\n\nSince `BuildOwner` already stamps `registrationDate = LocalDate.now()` on new owners, the 100 created in the test all count as \"today,\" and the 101st is rejected.\n\n**Tests:** full suite green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (creates 100, expects the 101st to be 429) passes.",
